& [ValidationSurface] is deterministic inspection only
  + exact CPPE form and Process IR versions are required
  + map keys, record identities, aggregate projections, and supplied cross-record references are checked
  + candidate purpose, scope, source representation, source digest, lifecycle, anchors, schemas, processes, bounds, effects, and retention are checked
  + every first-profile schema kind is required and all schemas remain closed
  + nested type and value depth, byte, collection, map, process, transition, message, event, queue, trace, and memory bounds are finite
  + process entry, terminal, successor, bound, operand, state, and continuation identities are checked
  + participant, frame, session, sender, receiver, message-kind, frame-generation, and token-pass relations are checked
  + validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue, revocation, invocation, result, trace, and fault record structure remains phase-distinct

& [CanonicalIdentity] is self-verifying
  + candidate source digest covers the exact selected source representation
  + schema-set digest covers the exact schema-set record with an empty self-digest placeholder
  + Process IR digest covers the complete IR record with an empty SHA-256 self-digest placeholder
  + compiled procedure digest covers its complete identity record with an empty SHA-256 self-digest placeholder
  + normalized aggregate and Process IR restoration rejects alternate whitespace, field order, unknown fields, stale versions, and content substitution

& [Corrections] preserve semantic meaning
  + ProcessInstanceState gains state_id because invocation plus process plus generation is a revision identity, not merely one process UUID
  + NegotiationSession gains session_generation_id so multiple immutable frame generations do not collide in the aggregate map
  + zero remaining budget is legal for a terminal or exhausted state while declared maximum bounds remain strictly positive
  + decimal bounds use canonical lexical form, declared scale, and signed magnitude ordering

& [DeliberateDeferral] is binding
  + CPPE-I03 owns source-form to IR lowering, source maps, diagnostics, cost estimates, and CompilationReceipt construction
  + I02 does not assert compiler success, verification, admission, catalogue mutation, execution, token-ring convergence, or external effects
  + no textual Simula parser, live provider, persistence, service, WASM, native backend, FPGA, or device behavior is implemented

& [SolutionDisposition] is accepted for CPPE-I02 after completed-work review
